Error [E2305]: this view points into `arena`, which this function owns
  --> tests/ui/arena_view_escape.jet:8:12
    |
  8 |     return x
    |            ^
 Why: `arena` is made here and freed when the function returns, so a read window into it would outlive what owns it — there'd be nothing left to look at
 Fix: return an owned copy with `~place` (for example `~value[a..b]`), or accept the source as a parameter so the caller keeps owning it

Error [E0631]: `x` cannot be shared — it does not live long enough to be returned
  --> tests/ui/arena_view_escape.jet:8:12
    |
  8 |     return x
    |            ^
 Why: `x` is a view into `arena`; sharing it outside the region would let it outlive `arena` and point into freed memory
 Fix: keep `x` inside the `arena` region, or copy what you need out with `~` before it leaves
